WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.390
February 2003.

2
00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.950
London starts charging drivers 5
pounds a day to drive in its centre.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.650
That year, excess delay in the zone
fell to 1.6 minutes per kilometre,

4
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.470
from a representative 2.3 in 2002.

5
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.830
By 2007, there were still 21 per cent
fewer vehicles with four or more wheels

6
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.550
than in 2002.

7
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.800
But excess delay was back to 2.3.

8
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:28.590
Less traffic, same congestion.

9
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.330
How?

10
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.890
Was the charge scrapped?

11
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.550
Did drivers ignore it?

12
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.650
In this mission, you'll measure congestion
the way Transport for London does,

13
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.870
in time and in space.

14
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.890
Then you'll judge whether
the charge succeeded,

15
00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.010
and test the baseline
it was measured against.

16
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:49.240
Your mission: explain how congestion could
come back while traffic stayed lower.
